{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.YLambdaClosedFormWenzlBridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.YLambdaClosedFormWenzlBridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.Factorial.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Sort","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":26,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzl_bridge_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzl_bridge_unique","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L233-L236","doc":"**Uniqueness — definitional compatibility alias.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzl_bridge_unique_categorical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzl_bridge_unique_categorical","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L216-L231","doc":"**Uniqueness — categorical layer.** Conditional on the\nChlouveraki 1-dim Markov-trace family axiom\n(`MarkovTraceFamilyOneDim`), any two normalised Markov traces on a\nHecke-algebra carrier `H` with parameter `jonesMarkovZ q` coincide,\nand the Wenzl-formula parameter pair `(Q, z_GL)` equals\n`(q², q · jonesMarkovZ q)` (`qou-z9fx`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzl_bridge_unique_definitional","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzl_bridge_unique_definitional","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L209-L214","doc":"**Uniqueness — definitional layer.** The convention iso\n`g = q σ` forces `wenzlQ q = q^2` and\n`wenzlZ q = q · jonesMarkovZ q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_closed_form_wenzl_bridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.y_lambda_closed_form_wenzl_bridge","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L189-L205","doc":"**Main theorem**: for `q > 1` in the σ-convention with convention-D\nMarkov parameter `z = q³/(q² + 1)`, the level-2 Jones-Markov central\ncoefficient `jonesMarkovCoefficient parts q lam` equals the Wenzl-bridge\nclosed form `yLambdaWenzlBridge parts lam q` at `Q = wenzlQ q = q²` and\n`X = wenzlX q = q·z/(1 - q² + q·z)`, with `1 < wenzlQ q`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge","label":"prop:y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jonesMarkovCoefficient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jonesMarkovCoefficient","kind":"def","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L181-L187","doc":"Central character coefficient of the Jones-Markov trace at\npartition `λ ⊢ n` in the explicit convention-D level-`r = 2`\nspecialisation `(Q, X) = (q², q⁴)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yLambdaWenzlBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.yLambdaWenzlBridge","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L169-L177","doc":"Closed-form Jones-Markov central coefficient `y_λ` via the\nWenzl bridge:\n  `y_λ(q) = s_{λ,r}(Q) / Z(Q)`\nwith `Q = wenzlQ q`, `X = wenzlX q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlNormalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlNormalization","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L164-L167","doc":"The total normalisation `Z = Σ_µ d_µ · s_{µ, r}(Q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlSchurElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlSchurElement","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L148-L162","doc":"The Wenzl principal-specialization Schur element for partition `λ ⊢ n`\nat parameter pair `(Q, X)` with `X = Q^r`:\n\n  `s_{λ,r}(Q) = Q^{n(λ)} · ∏_{(i,j) ∈ λ} (1 - X · Q^{c(i,j)}) / (1 - Q^{h(i,j)})`\n\ncomputed over all cells `(i, j)` of `lam.parts` (`qou-z9fx`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.nLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.nLambda","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L140-L144","doc":"Partition statistic `n(λ) = ∑_i i · λ_i` (0-indexed row index `i`),\nmatching `nPartition` in `y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean` (`qou-z9fx`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hookDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hookDim","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L130-L138","doc":"Number of standard Young tableaux of shape `λ` (= dimension of the\nirreducible `S_n`-representation `V_λ`), computed via the hook-length\nformula `f^λ = n! / ∏_{(i,j) ∈ λ} h(i, j)` (`qou-z9fx`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cellHook","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cellHook","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L119-L128","doc":"Hook length `h(i, j) = arm(i, j) + leg(i, j) + 1` for the cell at row `i`,\ncolumn `j` of a partition diagram (0-indexed), matching\n`y-lambda-recipe-from-partition.lean` (`qou-z9fx`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cellContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.cellContent","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L116-L117","doc":"Content `c(i, j) := j - i` for the cell at row `i`, column `j` (0-indexed). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.nonincr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.nonincr","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L114-L114","doc":"Non-increasing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.pos","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L112-L112","doc":"All parts positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L110-L110","doc":"Sum of parts equals `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.parts","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L108-L108","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L107-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.Partition","kind":"structure","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L106-L114","doc":"A partition of `n`: non-increasing positive ℕ-sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlX_eq_pow_four","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlX_eq_pow_four","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L88-L102","doc":"Under convention D (`z = q³/(q² + 1)`), the Wenzl bridge parameter\n`wenzlX q` collapses identically to `q⁴ = (wenzlQ q)²` (integer Wenzl\nlevel `r = 2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlX","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlX","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L81-L86","doc":"Explicit `X = Q^r = q·z / (1 - Q + q·z)`, solving the bridge\nequation `q · z = Q^r · (1 - Q) / (1 - Q^r)`. This is the\nuniversal substitution that turns Wenzl's Schur principal-\nspecialization formula into a closed q-rational expression. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlZ","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L77-L79","doc":"Convention-shifted Markov parameter `z_GL = q · z` in the\nWenzl/Orellana g-convention (eigenvalues `Q, -1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlQ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.wenzlQ","kind":"def","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L73-L75","doc":"Wenzl-convention variable `Q = q²` from the convention\nisomorphism `G = q σ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jonesMarkovZ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.jonesMarkovZ","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L67-L71","doc":"Markov parameter `z_D = q^3 / (q^2 + 1)` in the σ-convention used in\nthis paper (eigenvalues `q, -q⁻¹`) — **convention D**, canonical by the\nowner ruling of 2026-08-15 (R1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceFamilyOneDim.unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceFamilyOneDim.unique","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Any two Markov-trace functionals `tr₁ tr₂ : H → R` on a Hecke-algebra\ncarrier `H` (with unit `unit` and generator shift `appendGen`) that\nshare the Markov parameter `z` and normalisation `tr(unit) = 1`\nagree on every element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceFamilyOneDim.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceFamilyOneDim.mk","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceFamilyOneDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.MarkovTraceFamilyOneDim","kind":"class","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/y-lambda-closed-form-wenzl-bridge.lean#L45-L60","doc":"Local mirror of the categorical 1-dim Markov-trace family axiom\n(cf. `wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou.lean`, `prop:wenzl-bridge-applicability-qou`);\nboth encode Chlouveraki HDR Theorem 6.20 (= Juyumaya 2007 Theorem 12,\n`d = 1` case): the type-A Markov-trace family is one-dimensional in\nthe trace functionals, parameterised by `z` (`qou-z9fx`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}